  "plain": "A former Pentagon official turned whistleblower, Matthew Brown, says that from around 2018 reports of UAP, the government's term for unexplained flying objects, turned up very often in the intelligence he handled. He worked on stopping weapons of mass destruction, such as nuclear or chemical arms. If true, these sightings were a routine part of national security work rather than a rare oddity."
